  "schema": 3,
  "target_level": 3,
  "area": "3D engine and scanline timing",
  "about": "Expected result-block values for the Heddlemere rehearsal ROM and the release ROM's auto QA run, judged by tools/judge.py. Block layout: arm9/source/game/rehearsal.h (measurements: arm9/source/judge/timing.h). Timing values are cycles of the 33.51 MHz bus clock; \"x16\" values are fixed point with four fractional bits (the means of many lines or the slopes of two run lengths). Every measurement polls with IME = 0 and uses only differences, so interrupt latency cancels. \"frame\" is the minimum number of frames to run, per boot. Items of the measurement carry \"done\" on flags bit 0: every wait finished. \"known\" lists, per emulator version and renderer, the gating items expected to fail there; judge.py --profile passes only when the failing set matches exactly. GBATEK figures gate; the four items marked unconfirmed are those where GBATEK and melonDS disagree and wait for a measurement on hardware. hblank-low-arm9 (GBATEK 1606, melonDS 1584) is the fifth such item and informational for the same reason; its measurement is unbiased by a dithered delay (arm9/source/judge/timing.c). The cycle residual of a VCOUNT write is measured (values[8]) but not judged: it moves to probes/ with the apply line.",
  "block": {
    "address": "0x0237F000",
    "magic": 1380275779
  },
  "boots": {
    "rehearsal": {
      "rom": "heddlemere-rehearsal.nds",
      "item_id": 1213353288,
      "item_id_text": "HMRH",
      "frames": 3000,
      "note": "the timing measurements and a scripted play of the first order of every chapter; no save chip, no NitroFS"
    },
    "qa": {
      "rom": "heddlemere.nds",
      "item_id": 1314013521,
      "item_id_text": "QARN",
      "frames": 9000,
      "note": "the release ROM's hidden auto QA mode (title: hold L+R+X+Y for 120 frames): every order played, the credits, then the timing measurements once; the block uses the rehearsal's layout and adds the QA words at values[48..54] (verdict 1 PASS / 2 FAIL, log lines, SD flags, last state hash, checkpoints, lag, save flags)"
    }
  },
